Error [jet.UnknownFunction]: `Compiler` has no method `publish`
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:9:10
    |
  9 |     meta.publish(#code { extra: fn() -> Int { 2 } })
    |          ^^^^^^^
 Why: `Compiler` is a protected Core type with a closed method surface
 Fix: Write `meta.add(#code { ... }, scope: "name")`, `meta.add_struct("Name", fields, scope: "name")`, `meta.rewrite_body(f, #code { ... })`, `meta.allow_rewrite(package: "name")` or `meta.events(watch: .Functions{marked: Traced{}}, handler)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0102

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `Compiler.add` doesn't take this argument
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:10:66
    |
 10 |     meta.add(#code { extra: fn() -> Int { 2 } }, scope: "extra", 3)
    |                                                                  ^
 Why: `meta.add` takes one `Code` value or source text and the `scope:` module it joins
 Fix: Write `meta.add(#code { ... }, scope: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764

Error [jet.ArgumentCountMismatch]: `Compiler.add` expects a `Code` value or source text
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:11:10
    |
 11 |     meta.add(scope: "extra")
    |          ^^^
 Why: `meta.add` adds the items of one `Code` value or of source text
 Fix: Write `meta.add(#code { ... }, scope: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0104

Error [jet.ArgumentCountMismatch]: `Compiler.add` expects `scope:`
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:12:10
    |
 12 |     meta.add(#code { extra: fn() -> Int { 2 } })
    |          ^^^
 Why: The added items join the generated module `scope:` names
 Fix: Write `meta.add(#code { ... }, scope: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0104

Error [jet.ArgumentCountMismatch]: `Compiler.rewrite_body` expects a function and a `Code` value
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:13:10
    |
 13 |     meta.rewrite_body(helper)
    |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `meta.rewrite_body` replaces the body of one function with the statements of one `Code` value
 Fix: Write `meta.rewrite_body(f, #code { ... })`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0104

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `Compiler.rewrite_body` doesn't take this argument
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:14:31
    |
 14 |     meta.rewrite_body(helper, code: #code { 2 })
    |                               ^^^^
 Why: `meta.rewrite_body` takes a function's name and one `Code` value, both unlabeled
 Fix: Write `meta.rewrite_body(f, #code { ... })`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `meta.rewrite_body` needs a top-level function's name
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:16:23
    |
 16 |     meta.rewrite_body(count, #code { 2 })
    |                       ^^^^^
 Why: A body rewrite replaces the body of one top-level function, named directly, through its package, or by the `FunctionInfo` a `meta.events` handler hears
 Fix: Pass a top-level function, as in `meta.rewrite_body(f, #code { ... })` or `meta.rewrite_body(tool.f, #code { ... })`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `Compiler.allow_rewrite` takes one `package:` name
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:17:10
    |
 17 |     meta.allow_rewrite("greet")
    |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `meta.allow_rewrite` names the one dependency whose functions the value may rewrite
 Fix: Write `meta.allow_rewrite(package: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `meta.allow_rewrite` needs the package's name written out
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:19:24
    |
 19 |     meta.allow_rewrite(package: name)
    |                        ^^^^^^^
 Why: The consent is one line a reviewer reads, so it names its package as a string literal
 Fix: Write `meta.allow_rewrite(package: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764

Error [jet.UnknownArgumentLabel]: `meta.allow_rewrite` names `orm`, which is no package of this build
  --> tests/ui/meta_ladder_compiler_call_shapes.jet:20:24
    |
 20 |     meta.allow_rewrite(package: "orm")
    |                        ^^^^^^^
 Why: The consent covers one dependency this build loads, at its locked version
 Fix: Name a package listed in `deps:`, as in `meta.allow_rewrite(package: "name")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0764
